# Who has to approve what (per Isaac, Oct 2).
#
# The app's screens and logic (src/, engine/, styles, images) have NO owner:
# a developer's pull request that only touches those merges and deploys
# without waiting on anyone.
#
# The paths below run on the SERVER or during the BUILD, where the keys that
# reach QuickBooks, Windsor and the database live. A change to any of them
# needs Isaac's approval before it can merge (ruleset: "Require review from
# Code Owners"). That is the guardrail that keeps the P&L / QuickBooks data
# closed to anyone who can ship code.
/netlify/            @Isaachunter1
/netlify.toml        @Isaachunter1
/tools/              @Isaachunter1
/package.json        @Isaachunter1
/package-lock.json   @Isaachunter1
/migrations/         @Isaachunter1
/.github/            @Isaachunter1
